Ladybird exposes normal for the weight, style, and stretch of a CSS-
connected FontFace when the rule omits those descriptors. Font matching
uses the CSS initial values.

Chrome 158.0.8127.37, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 all returned normal
for omitted descriptors. Blink uses FontFace::weight(), style(), and
stretch(), Gecko uses FontFaceImpl::GetDesc(), and WebKit uses
FontFace::weight(), style(), and width().

For an explicitly declared auto, Chrome returned auto for all three
attributes. Firefox and WebKit returned normal. Ladybird preserves the
value the rule specifies.
